From: Reframed VR contributors
Subject: [PATCH] wsi/display: recognize an already held DRM master

Neo3's vendor kernel permits an unprivileged first opener to become master,
but requires privilege for both DROP_MASTER and SET_MASTER. After the ignored
drop failure during WSI initialization, the file is still master. Avoid a
redundant SET_MASTER that would otherwise reject a usable display file.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_display.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_display.c
@@ -1851,7 +1851,7 @@
       return 0;
 
    if (wsi->master_refcount++ == 0) {
-      int ret = drmSetMaster(wsi->fd);
+      int ret = drmIsMaster(wsi->fd) ? 0 : drmSetMaster(wsi->fd);
       if (ret != 0) {
          wsi_display_debug("drm fd %d failed to re-set master: %s", wsi->fd, strerror(-errno));
          wsi->master_refcount--;
